Rule 1 (dim must be within the valid range of dimensions to avoid IndexError)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1) ∨ (v_2 < 0 ∧ 0 - v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1))
>>
Rule 2 (when out is provided, its dtype must equal input dtype to avoid Float/Double and Complex dtype mismatches)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_3)
>>
Rule 3 (when out is provided, its shape must match input shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i)
>>
Rule 4 (input must have at least one dimension so a valid dim exists)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
